## Setup stops here, on one value: the address

Everything above is settled. One thing is not, and it is the one thing the framework will not let me guess or leave blank, because it is the value every future component copies.

Neither rule that derives an address fires here. This folder is not a git working copy and has no remote, and it does not sit inside a synced store — it is on `/tmp`. So, in the framework's words:

> This folder has no address yet, and a project needs one before I can set it up. Every folder you later add to this project keeps its own copy of this address, and that copy is how anyone working in one of those folders finds their way back here. So it has to be something that works from a different machine, rather than a path on this one.
>
> Two things count. A git remote you have pushed to, which gives an address like `https://github.com/you/pinewood-ceramics`. Or a folder inside a synced store — OneDrive, Google Drive, Dropbox — which gives one like `OneDrive, Projects/pinewood-ceramics`.
>
> `git init` on its own does not count. It gives this folder a history and leaves it in exactly one place, and what is being asked for is a second place.
>
> Set one of those up, or move the folder into one, and tell me when it is done. I will read the address from the folder rather than from your description. Until then there is nothing I can write, so setup stops here.

I have written no files. When the address exists, say so and I will re-resolve the path, put the summary table in front of you, and write `PROJECT.md`, `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` — nothing else is outstanding.
